# LANTERN: level 1 (OLD ENTRANCE) by lamplight: a crystal, two doors, a moth, the flash,
# the crank and the lift.
# Run: pocketme-sim --boot off --fps 60 --frames 1440 --script lantern.script
# (from boards/desktop). LANTERN starts at detail HEAVY (the whole-width view with
# textured floor and ceiling) and 60 pictures a second; the script keeps both.
# The walk is dead reckoning on the level's map; the game runs one tick a frame here.

# Home screen: six steps right, from BENCH to LANTERN, then start it.
10 press right
12 release right
16 press right
18 release right
22 press right
24 release right
28 press right
30 release right
34 press right
36 release right
40 press right
42 release right
56 press south
58 release south
140 press plus            # START plays level 1
142 release plus

200 press up             # east along the first tunnel, over a crystal (A CRYSTAL)
262 release up
266 press right          # face south
294 release right
300 press up             # down the side tunnel, a door on the left
340 release up
344 press left           # face the door (east)
372 release left
384 press south          # A: the door slides open
386 release south
450 press up             # through the door
490 release up
496 press right          # face south
524 release right
530 press up
570 release up
574 press left           # face the second door (east)
602 release left
612 press south          # A: it opens
614 release south
660 press up             # through it
700 release up
704 press left           # face north: a moth flies to the lamp
732 release left
# Still at 730: the moth close in front of the lamp, drinking its oil.
820 press east           # B: the flash; the moth flies off
822 release east

# On to the crank and the lift: east, south, west (the crank), south, east.
880 press right          # face east
908 release right
912 press up
952 release up
956 press right          # face south
984 release right
988 press up
1028 release up
1032 press right         # face west
1060 release right
1064 press up            # onto the crank (THE CRANK! FIND THE LIFT, about 1088)
1104 release up
1108 press left          # face south
1136 release left
1140 press up
1180 release up
1184 press left          # face east: the lift at the end of the tunnel
1212 release left
1216 press up
1256 release up
1264 press south         # A: the lift climbs, the level's card
1266 release south
